(version 1)

# Custom design rules for dst-01x4. KiCad reads `<board>.kicad_dru` from the board's own directory;
# Board Setup → Design Rules → Custom Rules is an editor for this file, so opening that dialog and
# pressing OK will write back whatever it has buffered.
#
# A custom rule beats the board-setup constraint for the thing it names. Where two rules match the
# same pair of objects, the *last* one in the file wins.
#
# No rules today. The board holds 0.2 mm hole-to-copper everywhere, and every land on it clears
# that; a relaxation scoped to one footprint's geometry is the shape a rule here would take.
